{"tool_name":"bioconda/proteomiqon-peptidespectrummatching","contents":["bioconda","galaxy"],"identifiers":["bioconda:proteomiqon-peptidespectrummatching","galaxy:proteomiqon_peptidespectrummatching"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"proteomiqon-peptidespectrummatching","version":"0.0.9","home":"https://csbiology.github.io/ProteomIQon/","documentation":"https://csbiology.github.io/ProteomIQon/tools/PeptideSpectrumMatching.html","license":"MIT","summary":"Given raw an MS run in the mzLite format, this tool iterates across all MS/MS scans, determines precursor charge states and possible peptide spectrum matches using reimplementations of SEQUEST, Andromeda and XTandem.","description":"Given raw a MS run in the mzLite or mzml format, this tool iterates accross all recorded MS/MS scans and determines the charge state of precursor \nions which were selected for fragmentation. With this it is possible to query the peptide data base for every precursor ion mass +/- a\ntolerance (which defines the so called 'search space') and retrieve peptides that are theoretical candidates for a match. For each of the peptide\ncandidates we create an theoretical spectrum in silico and compare it to the measured MS/MS scan.\n","build":{"noarch":"generic","number":0,"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"build":[null],"host":["unzip"],"run":["dotnet-runtime >=10.0, <11.0","zlib"]},"source_url":"https://www.nuget.org/api/v2/package/ProteomIQon.PeptideSpectrumMatching/0.0.9","test":{"commands":["test -x \"$PREFIX/bin/proteomiqon-peptidespectrummatching\"","test -f \"$PREFIX/lib/dotnet/tools/PeptideSpectrumMatching/ProteomIQon.PeptideSpectrumMatching.dll\"","bash -n \"$PREFIX/bin/proteomiqon-peptidespectrummatching\"","grep -q \"PeptideSpectrumMatching/ProteomIQon.PeptideSpectrumMatching.dll\" \"$PREFIX/bin/proteomiqon-peptidespectrummatching\""]}},"galaxy":{"version":"0.0.9","first_commit":"2021-07-15","conda_name":"\n                proteomiqon-peptidespectrummatching\n            ",